  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (2333.33) and comparing each outcome to it, then preferring the lottery with the higher probability of exceeding this level (which is Lottery A). However, the individual expresses a preference for aiming at a higher gain (4000) and considers the 80% chance acceptable, implying a preference for Lottery B. More importantly, there is no indication that the individual computed or used any form of average outcome as a reference point. The justification is based on aspiration in a colloquial sense (wanting more gain), not in the formal sense defined by the reason (a specific calculation of aspiration level). The information considered by the individual (higher gain, acceptable probability) does not match the structured comparison to an aspiration level. The rule of the reason (maximize probability of exceeding mean outcome) is not reflected in the verbal justification. Therefore, the individual did not use this formal aspiration-level reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
